                <pb facs="0166" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg67"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60i31/39: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Estonia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Carlson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tallinn</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-04-22T16:00:00+02:00">April 22, 1936—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 22—1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. Referring to Department’s telegram of April 11, 3 p.m., the Foreign Office
                    handed me today a note stating principally “The Estonian Government agree to
                    withdraw their proposal as far as it concerns the expiration of the Treaty and
                    as worded in the note of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to the American
                    Legation of May 21, 1935 (…)<anchor n="4a" xml:id="d36-f1"/>. At the same time
                    the Estonian Government, referring to the stipulations of Article 35 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">29</hi>] of the existing Treaty, confirm their desire to
                    modify the existing Treaty on May 22, 1937, at the latest”. Full text<anchor
                        n="5" xml:id="d36-f2"/> is being mailed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carlson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
